Z||000000||McJaded||10-10-2001||11:54 PM||||Alright so i broke my shifting cable and i'm down to two opptions buy a new aftermarket or take the one off my 4 cld. 84<P>The fiero i drive now is a 85 fiero se with a v6 3.1 (not 2.8) but linkage is the same will the 84's cable work on my  85 ? <P>spec. <BR>84 fiero 4 cl. se<BR>85 fiero 6 cl. se<P>please help me i'm in need i need my baby back <P>P.S i'm having shifting problems with all gears but the clutch isn't getting any stiffer and when my friend blew out is 84's clutch it just like locked up could both cables need replacing .. ?<P>------------------<BR>~*~McJaded~*~||||reg||11
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||03:16 PM||||Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The cable should fit I think. <P>What are your symptoms to make you think it is bad?? Your P.S. is confusing me. If the car will not go into gear with the engine running but goes fine with it off than the clutch is not releasing. The clutch slave cylinder may need bleeding. The clutch will always feel the same. It should not get any stiffer if it is going. It will just slip and the engine will be going at a different speed than the trans and the car will eventually just stop moving when you release the clutch. Go to <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch4.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch4.htm</A>  to see how to bleed the clutch slave.<P>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
